session:pr530Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #43 asked to replace the <details>-based collapsible class tree at /?view=classes with a Cytoscape + dagre hierarchical graph, per the existing plan in docs/plans/FRONTEND_PLAN.md. The existing showClassesView() function already fetched rdfs:subClassOf pairs via SPARQL and built a nested <details> DOM tree by hand; that whole render step was replaced with a Cytoscape.js instance laid out by the cytoscape-dagre extension, following the lazy CDN-load pattern already established by ensureCytoscape() for the query-result graph tab (issue #43's parent plan named the exact two extra CDN scripts to add: dagre and cytoscape-dagre). The one non-obvious decision was edge direction and dagre rankDir: since the data is child rdfs:subClassOf parent, keeping the edge source=child/target=parent but setting rankDir:'BT' (bottom-to-top) both preserves the semantically correct arrow direction (subclass -> superclass, the conventional reading) and produces the desired visual layout (superclasses on top, more specific classes below) without having to flip the edge direction just for layout purposes. A second decision was to cap the rendered hierarchy at 300 nodes with a warning banner, mirroring the pre-existing GRAPH_NODE_LIMIT pattern used by the query-result graph view, since a full-ontology class hierarchy has no natural LIMIT the user controls the way a SPARQL query result does. The pre-existing WebDriver test class_hierarchy_view_renders_subclass_tree asserted on DOM text inside #class-tree, which broke conceptually once rendering moved to a <canvas> (Cytoscape draws labels on canvas, invisible to .text()); it was rewritten to poll window.classCyInstance.nodes() instead, mirroring the window.cyInstance mirror pattern the query-result graph test already used. No CSP was found in sparql_endpoint that would block the new CDN scripts, and both new CDN URLs (dagre@0.8.5, cytoscape-dagre@2.5.0) were confirmed reachable via curl -I. No real browser/WebDriver was available in this environment, so the actual rendered layout and click-through navigation were not visually verified — only that the served HTML is well-formed and the WebDriver test compiles/skips cleanly without a driver, same as it did before this change." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:530 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr530 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
